85-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1364491#post1364491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, it's a line that several white wolf writers are ahead of me in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm?<br /> <br /> Did I miss the memo that someone was putting together a Beast 1.5e? Official or STV?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T01:40:23-08:00","id":1364496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1364493#post1364493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm?<br /> <br /> Did I miss the memo that someone was putting together a Beast 1.5e? Official or STV?</div> </div> </div> </div>ArcaneArts has referenced that it's on her list of things she wants to do (Reading that she wanted to is what sparked my brain going &quot;How would I do Beast?&quot; and then the 'tism took over) It's not what she's working on right now, but it's something she really wants to do.<br /> <br /> Granted, she's freelance, not staff. So nothing officially announced. But I went archive diving and<br /> <br /> &quot;I will happily admit here:<br /> How Beast can be reworked is one of my two major obsessions in terms of writing. I think I've missed the current pitch period, but I am <i>not </i>leaving Beast alone.<br /> <br /> And a lot of it is in line with the previous commentary you're referring, and in the same spirit-But <i>oh man </i>I want Beast.<br /> <br /> EDIT For Clarity: This does not mean anything is happening yet. I have nothing to report on the subject. I may end up never having anything to report on.<br /> <br /> But for now, the main follow-up is <i>yet</i>...&quot;<br /> <br /> So, as of now, nothing is happening. And what does happen is more likely to be integrating stuff from the PHB and making the whole thing more thematically coherent and less like 20 different writers were told to go with no oversight. Definitely nothing as dramatic as what I'm working on.. But there is desire on that front.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm fairly certain I've seen other writers on the forum say they wanted to do something similar. That's just the one I remembered and could look for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10984,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","user":"Neckbeard the Pirate","date":".  forgot a point 02-01-2020, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T01:48:07-08:00","id":1364498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neckbeard the Pirate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1364496#post1364496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, she's freelance, not staff. So nothing officially announced.</div> </div> </div> </div>...and that has completely different and misleading connotations then the term &quot;white wolf writers&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T02:00:56-08:00","id":1364500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1364498#post1364498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...and that has completely different and misleading connotations then the term &quot;white wolf writers&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I misunderstood something then forgive me. I thought she did work for OPP, and that made her &quot;a white wolf writer.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T02:03:17-08:00","id":1364501,"title":"","content":"So serious question:<br /> <br /> What's the appeal of this to people that like Changeling the Lost already?<br /> <br /> The Dark Mother is now more like a Keeper snatching humans up and twisting them into inhuman things. The main Lost antagonists are more equals (or worse) as either fellow lost, Hedge beings, or the Huntsmen. Wyrd is a double-edged sword that helps you actualize your self but risks bringing you closer to your Keepers designs. Etc.<br /> <br /> The pitch leaves me wondering where the uniqueness is.<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> On the whole writer terminology thing.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path and White Wolf/Paradox Interactive are two different companies. Working for Onyx Path doesn't mean you're working for White Wolf, even if you're working on a property WW owns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 02-01-2020, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T02:24:32-08:00","id":1364505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1364501#post1364501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So serious question:<br /> <br /> What's the appeal of this to people that like Changeling the Lost already?<br /> <br /> The Dark Mother is now more like a Keeper snatching humans up and twisting them into inhuman things. The main Lost antagonists are more equals (or worse) as either fellow lost, Hedge beings, or the Huntsmen. Wyrd is a double-edged sword that helps you actualize your self but risks bringing you closer to your Keepers designs. Etc.<br /> <br /> The pitch leaves me wondering where the uniqueness is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Serious answer: Thank you, because that's a really helpful question to ask. <br /> <br /> As of now, the main difference between Changeling and what I have here is theme. Changeling is, at the risk of being reductionist, PTSD the game. You've come back from something traumatic, and now you're just trying to rebuild your life. Or build a new one. What I'm going for here is that the traumatic thing is happening now. I'm trying to capture the idea that being a beast is a lot like being tied to a railroad track and you can see the train coming. You've been cast in a narrative where your role has been decided for you and everything is building up to your eventual downfall, and while you can stave that off, you can't exactly stop it.<br /> <br /> Also pacing is a big thing. Changeling is very much a slow burn. There's a lot of paranoia. Not knowing who you can or can't trust. This version of Beast is intended to play a lot like a roller coaster. Your legend is growing. In fact, it's probably growing pretty fast. The higher it gets, the more fucked you are. In Changeling, you spend xp to increase your wyrd when you want to. Your legend is growing whether you like it or not, and it's growing at a fairly fast pace compared to most supernaturals and their power stats. And it's honestly intended to be less of a double edged sword and more of a burden than most things. Like yes, okay, as legend grows, you become &quot;more powerful.&quot; But &quot;More Powerful&quot; in this context doesn't really help you to do anything more than be a more terrifying beast. As a changeling, a higher wyrd is helpful for your stated goal of &quot;re-integrate into the real world and build a new life for myself, and avoid going back to arcadia&quot; because your contracts help you to do that. As a beast, your higher levels of power are kind of intended to feel hollow. In the sort of fun way that power is generally not worth it in the Chronicles of Darkness, and we all play this game because we kind of like playing out fucked situations and trying to fight our way out of or through them. <br /> <br /> Or at least that's what I'm going for. I think you are right that mechanically, this needs some tweaking to make it more unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T03:03:26-08:00","id":1364509,"title":"","content":"So... what's the point of asking, &quot;are you going to lie there and let him,&quot; if you're tied down anyway?<br /> <br /> It feels like you're getting too narrow in your design to the point where it's going to start feeling like a module for some larger game than a complete game in and of itself. You're, um, railroading your Beasts onto a very specific narrative, saying they should be defiant, but then hobbling all of their methods of defiance. The pacing aspect certainly isn't helping from a game-play perspective. How are players supposed to actualize standing up and not taking it, if they're shoved to the end too fast to really do much?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T07:02:18-08:00","id":1364531,"title":"","content":"*rubs the bridge of her nose*<br /> <br /> I have the feeling this thread is going to give me a headache later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T07:17:36-08:00","id":1364532,"title":"","content":"if I may ask, why is the dark mother so...direct in this one? she seems almost like a hyper-focused god machine. why the shift away from a truly atavistic being?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T11:37:41-08:00","id":1364570,"title":"","content":"I'm not feeling this. Like at first it seems like a variant where the Guardian Beasts from the Players Guide's beliefs are fact. Save that instead of the Dark Mother being a neglectful parent, she abducts kids to throw in a pit and have knife fights with Thunderdome rules.<br /> <br /> There's also a level of hopelessness to the scenario I'm not feeling. The Dark Mother is essentially a god in this and she's active, focused, and capable of operating on small scales. You can't win against this thing, or even oppose it in a meaningful way because if you get too close to its weight class I can't see why it won't just crush you into a mushy paste. Basically you're playing Deviant, except your Progenitor is a God with the resources and powers of such.<br /> <br /> Heroes are well not entertaining. Like I get the idea you want them to be threats, but you've gone about it in a way that's more likely to get the ST punched in the face for than praised. The way their built means the game would need to function like Elder Scrolls:Oblivion as you wouldn't be able to risk becoming powerful since it would passively boost your enemies. Which of course also means you can't oppose the big bad because they can always just create more Heroes and the stronger you get the stronger they are immediately.<br /> <br /> Not to mention the bit about seeking the Dark Mother's blessing because the fear of this thing gets too great, has two options as I see it. One the Dark Mother is a known deity to the world active churches to the Dark Mother all over and such and shrines etc. Which means you've got churches and such to The Idea of Evil from Berserk.* Which would still be preferable to the option where this implies the Dark Mother is actually the God people pray to in most religions. Trust me I had so much railing from some players just on Demon just because Soul Pacts are titled as such even if they have nothing to do with it; it would not have ended well if the game gave enough evidence that it implied their religion was actually worshiping an entity that directly causes untold pain, suffering, and misery because our species can't not be worried about something.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Actually considering this whole cycle is based on trying to relieve the fact that humans are bleeding worry worts and the solution is to create monsters to fear as a source for those worries it is The Idea of Evil from Berserk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T17:00:12-08:00","id":1365138,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with nalak42, specially when it came to Heroes, just reading about your idea when it involves Heroes makes me ask, why would I play a game like that? just thinking about playing like that becomes frustrating in my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T15:43:20-08:00","id":1365381,"title":"","content":"Thirded. Demons are constantly on the run or hiding, but the thing is that they're really <i>good </i>at being on the run or hiding, and they only get better at it. And turning from hunted to hunter when they have the opportunity. So it doesn't feel disempowering, only really tense.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it doesn't need a partial rewrite, but I'd go with the idea that Heroes and Beasts feed on each other; Heroes abusing someone who isn't naturally a latent Beast can result in them calling for anyone to help, and the Dark Mother answers; her offer is to fuse with a Horror and be adopted, but her price is to fundamentally accept you are defining yourself in opposition to Heroes, one of the furious marauders at the gates. However, with the acceptance it is fundamentally a cycle of abuse, comes the capacity to break it, and turn Heroes back into Oracles (Dark Eras 2; that's what they're supposed to be, but Egyptian Beasts fucked it up).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T22:00:27-08:00","id":1373326,"title":"","content":"So it's been a month plus change since this first gave me a headache, but I feel I can't have mentioned that headache without <i>eventually</i> commenting on it, so:<br /> <br /> 1) Thank you, by the way, for the default female pronoun. That's probably going to become the mainstay here soon. Might become the mainstay all over the board of life, but that's a different subject, but odds are my online self is going to just be female.<br /> <br /> 2) So. Like. Here's the <i>thing</i> about any rewrite about Beast:<br /> <br /> With <i>possibly one exception</i>, and that's one I bat back and forth on <i>a lot</i>, and frequently bat with Cinder on, the main thing to understand about Beast is that....all the materials for making a great Beast are <i>there</i>. You don't have to <i>change</i> much about the fundamental elements of Beast. What <i>needs changing</i> is the presentation and the order of operations. Beast is a game about Building Your Lair (your presence in the psycho-spiritual landscape of humanity in a meaningful way) which you do by sating your Hunger that build your rumors and whispers, bind the Chambers of tragedy and the particular mythos of your fellows through Kinship to your image, and fight off the Heroes (and Insatiable) who challenge your transcendent image (here read as &quot;personal values and means of self-identification as communicated in the medium of horror&quot;).<br /> <br /> Lair=Hunger+Chambers+Kinship+Opposition. That's the game in a nutshell, and it's Darkly Scion With Weirdness and Transmittable Mutability is damnedably strong on it's own.<br /> <br /> Putting it bluntly and shortly, the main failing of Beast right now is that Matthew McFarland <i>fucked up*</i> taking this really simple formula and delivering in a really cool, cohesive, and positively controversial way. The mice will play whatever they want when the cat was away, and in this case the cat was clearly away at a bunch of different houses.<br /> <br /> Beast <i>has</i> everything it needs to be awesome. It just needs to be lined up and presented the right way, with the correct unity of vision on the material, to be properly seen. Supplements from there just need to build outward in a way that is progressingly fun to play, terrifying to consider, and weird to comprehend.<br /> <br /> I'll leave the &quot;exception&quot; unexplained as an interesting batting experiment.<br /> <br /> *Okay, maybe not fucked up, I think Matt did <i>enough</i> good in fixing things up and directing it, and the writers inserted enough diverse and interesting text(even to it's detriment) that there's a clear reason Beast has it's fanbase. But for those of us who got into Beast, once we got away from the feeling that was right, that spoke to us, it's not hard to see how the text is a fairly sloppy stitched together animal with weeping wounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-07-2020, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T11:25:05-08:00","id":1373409,"title":"","content":"Arcane speaks truth.<br /> <br /> Thinking on what I wrote, the two major rules changes I would make are &quot;Oracles are in the core&quot; and &quot;there's a social z-axis.&quot;<br /> <br /> For the first, I'd have it explicit a Hero is a berserk Oracle. They haven't all gone out, probably not the majority of Oracles are Heroes. However, society encourages Oracles to become Heroes and helps Heroes get stuck in an emotional rut. What really makes a Hero a Hero isn't some inborn impulse to hunt Beasts, but believing that their own Dream sense is telling them to destroy it rather than study it. An Oracle who knows, and more importantly accepts, what her power is telling her can still turn on Beasts, but that's because the Beasts in question pissed her off. More than a few of the most dangerous Heroes in the world are actually Oracles who work as a team with hunters, and regularly seek and destroy Beasts who they feel are polluting the Dream with toxic nightmares of abuse and not controlling themselves.<br /> <br /> For the second, that gives both a social aspect to the whole thing and also puts the Beast Player's Guide social groups in the core, which is a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T16:34:22-08:00","id":1373453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1373326#post1373326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lair=Hunger+Chambers+Kinship+Opposition. That's the game in a nutshell, and it's Darkly Scion With Weirdness and Transmittable Mutability is damnedably strong on it's own.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Arc's whole post is a gem, but I'll quote this part since I feel to elaborate a little, because why not.<br /> <br /> This formula here is on point and it's pretty much the key to unlock the magic. As Arc said, that's the game in a nutshell, which allows for a huge range of possibilities &amp; stories. A range, I dare to say, which belongs to Beast first and foremost and other games don't cover in the same way.<br /> <br /> (Which is alright, Beast can't do as well things other gamelines do easily and each one should have its strengths. To think otherwise...is not the best thing)<br /> <br /> Beast, with that in mind, just is this <i>weird </i>game about fears, hopes, actions, and consequences, with its own gnarly language to talk about all of those. No matter the scale of the story it's always deeply intimate.<br /> <br /> You can have a sorta-Pulp chronicle where you travel across the world looking for artifacts and tracks of the Dark Mother.<br /> <br /> You can have a game where the monsters from a book start to haunt the town because some kids opened it on Halloween night and the Brood must clean up the mess.<br /> <br /> You can have the kind of crossover game which requires my weight in books, with allies &amp; foes from all gamelines woven together into the Beast's legend.<br /> <br /> You can have a game of mythical resonance, with heroes and horrors who fight one against each other, each strike reverberating in the Astral.<br /> <br /> You can have a Tier 4 game where old gods awaken, the Dark Mother opens the gates, and Gaia stirs in her slumber.<br /> <br /> And you can have your Tier 0 game, where flawed individuals fight to tell their own story, one day at a time. With blood, pain, and no easy answers.<br /> <br /> The only thing we need is to take steps to see that more clearly. Supplement after supplement, with a strong guiding vision behind. There's lots of stuff we need to be able to see better. The vast world connected through Lairs, the mysteries of the Dark Mother &amp; the Primordial condition, the kind of stories one can tell, the actual immensity of the Begotten's crooked family tree...the list goes on.<br /> <br /> Also, Beast is the Astral gameline. The Begotten are living stories and have a role in our world no other Astral-related phenomenon has. <i>They're the children of Fear</i>. Let's see how cool that can be, let's explore the facets of that universe, let's have astral gods and Dreamborn show up to try and have their role in the story, whether the Begotten would like it or not.<br /> <br /> The supplements after the core are doing a great job. Conquering Heroes and the Player's Guide were awesome, and I say this with renewed vigor because I just reread them. The Geryo connection in Shunned by the Moon is cool as fuck and ripe with story fodder. The Dark Eras 2 Beast sections are solid, useful, and <i>good</i>.<br /> <br /> The fire is there and it's alive. It just needs to be presented better, so it can breathe, grow, and burn brighter. Hopefully we'll get there.<br /> <br /> God, I love this game. This dark mixture of mythology, psychology, empathy, hunger, folklore, acceptance, conflict, growth, mistakes, regrets, and aspirations.<br /> <br /> I know this reply is kinda superfluous, but I was in the right mood for it.<br /> <br /> P.S. That one exception does need some batting, because it's an important element. But, by Nightmare Mom, I'm not giving up on that. Also, Arc knows what she says and I'm thankful I get to chat with her about Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-07-2020, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T17:05:13-08:00","id":1373458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1373453#post1373453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arc's whole post is a gem, but I'll quote this part since I feel to elaborate a little, because why not.<br /> <br /> This formula here is on point and it's pretty much the key to unlock the magic. As Arc said, that's the game in a nutshell, which allows for a huge range of possibilities &amp; stories. A range, I dare to say, which belongs to Beast first and foremost and other games don't cover in the same way.<br /> <br /> (Which is alright, Beast can't do as well things other gamelines do easily and each one should have its strengths. To think otherwise...is not the best thing)<br /> <br /> Beast, with that in mind, just is this <i>weird </i>game about fears, hopes, actions, and consequences, with its own gnarly language to talk about all of those. No matter the scale of the story it's always deeply intimate.<br /> <br /> You can have a sorta-Pulp chronicle where you travel across the world looking for artifacts and tracks of the Dark Mother.<br /> <br /> You can have a game where the monsters from a book start to haunt the town because some kids opened it on Halloween night and the Brood must clean up the mess.<br /> <br /> You can have the kind of crossover game which requires my weight in books, with allies &amp; foes from all gamelines woven together into the Beast's legend.<br /> <br /> You can have a game of mythical resonance, with heroes and horrors who fight one against each other, each strike reverberating in the Astral.<br /> <br /> You can have a Tier 4 game where old gods awaken, the Dark Mother opens the gates, and Gaia stirs in her slumber.<br /> <br /> And you can have your Tier 0 game, where flawed individuals fight to tell their own story, one day at a time. With blood, pain, and no easy answers.<br /> <br /> The only thing we need is to take steps to see that more clearly. Supplement after supplement, with a strong guiding vision behind. There's lots of stuff we need to be able to see better. The vast world connected through Lairs, the mysteries of the Dark Mother &amp; the Primordial condition, the kind of stories one can tell, the actual immensity of the Begotten's crooked family tree...the list goes on.<br /> <br /> Also, Beast is the Astral gameline. The Begotten are living stories and have a role in our world no other Astral-related phenomenon has. <i>They're the children of Fear</i>. Let's see how cool that can be, let's explore the facets of that universe, let's have astral gods and Dreamborn show up to try and have their role in the story, whether the Begotten would like it or not.<br /> <br /> The supplements after the core are doing a great job. Conquering Heroes and the Player's Guide were awesome, and I say this with renewed vigor because I just reread them. The Geryo connection in Shunned by the Moon is cool as fuck and ripe with story fodder. The Dark Eras 2 Beast sections are solid, useful, and <i>good</i>.<br /> <br /> The fire is there and it's alive. It just needs to be presented better, so it can breathe, grow, and burn brighter. Hopefully we'll get there.<br /> <br /> God, I love this game. This dark mixture of mythology, psychology, empathy, hunger, folklore, acceptance, conflict, growth, mistakes, regrets, and aspirations.<br /> <br /> I know this reply is kinda superfluous, but I was in the right mood for it.<br /> <br /> P.S. That one exception does need some batting, because it's an important element. But, by Nightmare Mom, I'm not giving up on that. Also, Arc knows what she says and I'm thankful I get to chat with her about Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus fuck is this all true.<br /> <br /> Cinder is THE BEAST GUY","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-08T01:12:02-08:00","id":1373498,"title":"","content":"&quot;-Satiety is reworked into a more traditional fuel source, a la vitae, essence, glamour, etc.&quot;<br /> <br /> Forgive me if I missed a comment on this earlier, but frickin WHY? If anything, I think more fuel stats need to have effects beyond &quot;full = good empty = bad.&quot; I'd want more gamelines to have fuel stats that produce a sense of tension and have associated effects, not less.<br /> <br /> Re: heroes, while its easy for a prepared beast to zap them, with 2 atavisms and 2 lair traits, its inconvenient for every beast to be ready for them at all times. I would have there be some sort of rare &quot;greater hero&quot; that can 1v1 beasts, but mostly I feel the threat of an angry mob coming for you is good enough on its own. The entire game doesn't have to be defined by innate drawbacks.<br /> <br /> Also its part of the charm that the Dark Mother can be cast as loving towards beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-08T04:39:51-07:00","id":1373527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1373498#post1373498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: heroes, while its easy for a prepared beast to zap them, with 2 atavisms and 2 lair traits, its inconvenient for every beast to be ready for them at all times. I would have there be some sort of rare &quot;greater hero&quot; that can 1v1 beasts, but mostly I feel the threat of an angry mob coming for you is good enough on its own. The entire game doesn't have to be defined by innate drawbacks.</div> </div> </div> </div> One way I've had bouncing around to deal with this is to give Heroes the (somewhat unreliable) ability to steal Atavisms or Nightmares from Beasts they defeat, either personally or by proxy. Consider the arrows of Herakles, dipped in the venom of the Lernaean Hydra or the armor he made from the skin of the Nemean Lion. There's also some potential there for Beasts giving power to Oracles willingly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T10:38:47-07:00","id":1373782,"title":"","content":"Just want to say I'm happy to have read all the creative criticism and commentary in this thread. It helped me rethink my feelings about Beast a lot without kicking the same dead horses again and again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T16:50:21-07:00","id":1373816,"title":"","content":"<i>Your Mother needs you.</i><br /> <br /> Beyond the abuser thing, one thing that's struck me about Beast is its lack of an &quot;epic struggle&quot; concept. Almost every other &quot;splat&quot; has an epic side to it along with the individual, day-to-day struggles.<br /> <br /> The Forsaken are the inheritors of Father Wolf, forced to take up his task after killing him for the good of reality, even against Lovecraftian nightmares like the Idigam.<br /> <br /> Mages have the task of closing the Abyss and Awakening the whole of humanity.<br /> <br /> Prometheans spend their existence struggling to becoming something that fits into a Natural Order that constantly rejects them.<br /> <br /> Changelings live with the constant fear that the True Fae, the monsters who abducted, abused and enslaved them will drag them back to their special hells in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Hunters are people realizing that they live in a world of darkness and monsters.<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters ultimately want to reboot the Afterlife.<br /> <br /> Demons are trying avoid/resist the God who is a Machine.<br /> <br /> Mummies are torn between the screaming demands or otherworldly Judges as they try to understand who they were and wish to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even Vampires who are in some ways a lot like Beasts in terms of feeding a demanding Hunger, face a kind of epic struggle in terms of the vampire vs. The System. Every vampire from the newest Neonate to the most ancient of Elders is forced by Kindred society to fit into places that that society defines, to play a game whose rules were set (and rigged against you) millennia ago.<br /> <br /> With Beasts... they need to feed their Hungers. For Ruin. For Prey For other things. They use Nightmares and Atavisms. They build their Lairs. So they can better feed their Hungers. Some grow potent enough to became their Legends Incarnate... so they can feed their Hungers. And... that seems to be it. Sure Heroes crop up and the Insatiable are problematic, to say the least. Others in the world aren't necessarily friendly, but over all there doesn't seem to be much of a calling for Beasts as a whole beyond, than get fed, but not too well fed.<br /> <br /> Looked at in some ways, Beast is basically the &quot;darker, edgier&quot; version of Monsters, Inc. with the PCs being a bunch of Sullys going out to make sure their personal &quot;power plants&quot; don't run out of juice.<br /> <br /> So let's consider changing that up a little.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Because the time is coming...</i><br /> <br /> We have Lilith, the Dark Mother. Except that Lilith seems mostly irrelevant. Father Wolf casts a much longer shadow over the Forsaken than Lilith does over the Begotten despite him being dead for thousands of years. So, Lilith, the Dark Mother. If there's a Mother, is there a Father. And for my purposes the answer is Yes. Oh yes. And things are so much worse than you might think.<br /> <br /> ...when He will wake up.<br /> <br /> So, let's spin the myth a little.<br /> '<br /> <i>In the Times Before, They were.<br /> <br /> Two They were. He and She.<br /> <br /> They made the world or found the world or were the world.<br /> <br /> They loved and made and played<br /> <br /> Until the Machine Thing came from Elsewhere.<br /> <br /> It tried to take their world for a Purpose of its own.<br /> <br /> They fought It. They damaged it but He was wounded.<br /> <br /> Wounded. Poisoned. Maddened. He fell.<br /> <br /> Into an Abyss. He was the Abyss. <br /> <br /> She could not help Him and had to flee.<br /> <br /> To retreat into the Great Priomordial Dream.<br /> <br /> The Machine forgot Her and Him. Forgot its Purpose.<br /> <br /> It still Made and Meddled and Experiementec trying to find<br /> <br /> what it Lost and time over time its damage grew.<br /> <br /> He lived. The Wound did not kill Him.<br /> <br /> The Poison did not kill Him.<br /> <br /> The Madness did not leave Him. <br /> <br /> And He slept. Uneasily. <br /> <br /> And He dreamed. Terrible Things.<br /> <br /> Time passed. She watched the world change.<br /> <br /> She watched the monkeys lose their fur and grow their minds.<br /> <br /> And She loved them in her way.<br /> <br /> And She feared for them. Feared for Her world.<br /> <br /> Because He slept, but only slept.<br /> <br /> In His dreams He came to Her and they made...<br /> <br /> children together. And She loved the children,<br /> <br /> Horrors though they were.<br /> <br /> But She did not sleep. Could not rest<br /> <br /> She was the Mother now. She watched over all her children<br /> <br /> Even while the addled Machine did its Purposeless work<br /> <br /> She could touch the world. Lightly. Carefully<br /> <br /> She whispered to the Spirits.<br /> <br /> She whispered to some of the Humans, letting them see Beyond<br /> <br /> to Touch the Higher if only briefly<br /> <br /> But to some souls she gave her greatest gift.<br /> <br /> Her Children. Her Horrors. Her Hungers.<br /> <br /> To them she was Lilith<br /> <br /> And they loved their Mother<br /> <br /> They would Feed and as they Fed<br /> <br /> They would Forge the spirit of humanity<br /> <br /> Shape it with Pain and Fear and Loss<br /> <br /> Make it stronger. Make it ready. For Him.<br /> <br /> Because she was so very tired.<br /> <br /> And weakened. Her Begooten help her.<br /> <br /> They Feed her as they Feed.<br /> <br /> But she grows weak and she needs to sleep.<br /> <br /> But she cannot. She must not.<br /> <br /> Because the time is coming<br /> '<br /> When He, when Typhon will Awaken<br /> <br /> And devour.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T17:21:52-07:00","id":1373817,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2318\" data-vbnamecard=\"2318\">johntfs</a> Beasts, in my opinion have an epicness on building their Legend and asserting that they are their own person when a Hero tells them they are nothing more than monsters to be slain. Not only that, but their are whole hives of Beasts that can be conquered and made your own. And to be fair on Vampire, that's really mostly a Carthian experience. If you're Invictus, it will be about using that Establishment to your advantage.<br /> <br /> I wont lie though, the game could better present this aspect of the game, what with beasts being THE gameline presenting the Astral, the collective conscious of all humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T17:22:51-07:00","id":1373818,"title":"","content":"I feel like the &quot;epicifying&quot; of Beast misses a few things-partly in how local all of the games actually are how that epic angle misses that, and also Not All Mages Care About the Abyss(Arguably, just the Guardians and the Mysterium make it a Big Ass Deal, everyone else is like &quot;Yeah, okay, but EXARCHS&quot;-<br /> <br /> But mostly it also does hit on something that is true about Beast....even if it doesn't need all of ^that.<br /> <br /> Because Again, Beast is a Darkly Scion game. It's a game about Building Your Legend, which by the way eventually births a new world as that Lair grows. The Astral is the place where you will actually <i>find</i> your mythologies come to life, and is thus loaded with your Sets and your Odins and your Tezcatlipocas (although archetypalism and formalism remains king, so it's confronting Sage and Mountain and hey did anyone else realize that Beast is the second game to be most keenly interested in Pangaeans in this way?)-the game is loaded with Astral Gods and Demons to confront and get involved in. This is a game where it is appropriate to say you become a deity at it's higher levels, and that's not accounting for the ways Inheritances are psychospiritually huge ass deals.<br /> <br /> It's mostly self-directed, mind-the game doesn't implore you pit yourself against anything <i>directly</i> in the way the other games do-but on the other hand, it really does, because it basically asks you to become bigger than the world itself, and even gives you the tools for it. Beast is a game where as you rise, you should feel it, can even see it-all the world, turning in your direction. Beast is the game where you get to answer the question &quot;I ask of thee!- Art thou humanity?&quot; with &quot;Nay! I am the world-the world inside the gourd.&quot; It's a game of chaoskampf against forces all interested in building <i>their own</i> worlds, and it absolutely ratchets up to that point.<br /> <br /> Now a lot more of that can be shined up and bought to the forefront in the text and even supported mechanically (Looking at you, supplements), but it is <i>there</i>. It just has to actually be <i>understood</i> that way.<br /> <br /> But no, Typhon is fine on his throne.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-10-2020, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T17:49:02-07:00","id":1373822,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, worth noting, Beast also contends with and against every mythic element of every other gameline, and even has reason to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T19:18:54-07:00","id":1373829,"title":"","content":"I would even say the path to Incarnation is perhaps the area where Beast has improved the most from kickstarter pitch to the material in the Players Guide. Killing a Hero without taking damage is something Lair 8 Beasts can probably do by accident, which is a pretty anticlimactic path to godhood, but the other options are pretty tall orders that require making the world really listen to your story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T20:02:02-07:00","id":1373834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1373822#post1373822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, worth noting, Beast also contends with and against every mythic element of every other gameline, and even has reason to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn Arcane, Cinder may be my favourite for essays on Beast, but you're a real close second. Are you making that 1.5 edition for the storyteller vault? I would really like to read it if it involves the Astral (and that would make feel a lot better about building your Legend and how the Horror itself spreads through the collective unconscious of humanity.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T00:29:06-07:00","id":1373856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1373816#post1373816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Beasts... they need to feed their Hungers. For Ruin. For Prey For other things. They use Nightmares and Atavisms. They build their Lairs. So they can better feed their Hungers. Some grow potent enough to became their Legends Incarnate... so they can feed their Hungers. And... that seems to be it. Sure Heroes crop up and the Insatiable are problematic, to say the least. Others in the world aren't necessarily friendly, but over all there doesn't seem to be much of a calling for Beasts as a whole beyond, than get fed, but not too well fed.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's that? I'm sorry, it's a bit difficult hearing you over all the roaring I'm doing, building up my legend of being a motherfucking<i> dragon</i> all up in this town.<br /> <br /> So, something about lack of an &quot;epic struggle&quot;? I mean, if all you've got to do on your Sunday nights is watching football then I find it hard to relate. Heroes are sometimes a concern, yeah, usually when some genius suddenly thinks they've got a chance to be St. George. But as a dragon, you'll find that if you just get angry enough, a hell of a lotta things will BURN. However, fending off Heroes isn't where I get my entertainment from. <br /> <br /> Naw, man, <i>exploring </i>is the thing! You think all that Kin have something fascinating by having other dimensions or realities to deal with? Yeah, none of those doors are shut to <i>ME</i>. If it's a gateway, a portal, a tear, I'm shoving my snout way up in that doorway with a roar of, &quot;Knock, knock!&quot; and shouldering my way through. No invitation required for <i>my </i>draconic personage! You see, the secrets of those other places aren't denied to me. And they're all mine for the taking! All sorts of lost knowledge and I can add it all to my library, my treasure trove of....<br /> <br /> ...Wait a second, hold on.<br /> <br /> H-hey! You, wizard looking dude! What the bloody hell do you think you're doing in my library?! You think you can stick your nose in my business without my say-so? ...Oh, don't you dare give me any lip on my turf, little mageling! You think I won't use my fire among my precious books? Things here <i>only </i>burn when I want them to burn, and you're looking awfully flammable to me right now! ...Yeah, I thought you'd reconsider. You want some of my secrets, you gotta pay for it upfront, buddy. I have library cards for that reason.<br /> <br /> Now, where was I?<br /> <br /> Oh, right. On top of managing my library of supernatural secrets and forbidden knowledge, I also have a side gig built up from being active in my local community of monsters. I don't just go places, I can also let people through as well! And beyond that, my blood has got <i>power </i>to it. Those wizards and sorcerers love having me attend their workings, and with a bit of a bloody blessing from me, they've got a lot more dark power to draw upon. Even the werewolves have their own little rituals they observe. Oh, I've gotten some juicy lore from the Shadow in exchange for my help when one of those wolf shamans needed some extra draconic OOMPH to their ritual to kick a spirit's hiney outta here that was more than they could manage on their own.<br /> <br /> So, yes. Considering the evidence of being a <i>fucking</i> dragon, I can only conclude that your argument looks invalid to me. Rawr, baby. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T03:01:25-07:00","id":1373872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1373856#post1373856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's that? I'm sorry, it's a bit difficult hearing you over all the roaring I'm doing, building up my legend of being a motherfucking<i> dragon</i> all up in this town.<br /> <br /> So, something about lack of an &quot;epic struggle&quot;? I mean, if all you've got to do on your Sunday nights is watching football then I find it hard to relate. Heroes are sometimes a concern, yeah, usually when some genius suddenly thinks they've got a chance to be St. George. But as a dragon, you'll find that if you just get angry enough, a hell of a lotta things will BURN. However, fending off Heroes isn't where I get my entertainment from.<br /> <br /> Naw, man, <i>exploring </i>is the thing! You think all that Kin have something fascinating by having other dimensions or realities to deal with? Yeah, none of those doors are shut to <i>ME</i>. If it's a gateway, a portal, a tear, I'm shoving my snout way up in that doorway with a roar of, &quot;Knock, knock!&quot; and shouldering my way through. No invitation required for <i>my </i>draconic personage! You see, the secrets of those other places aren't denied to me. And they're all mine for the taking! All sorts of lost knowledge and I can add it all to my library, my treasure trove of....<br /> <br /> ...Wait a second, hold on.<br /> <br /> H-hey! You, wizard looking dude! What the bloody hell do you think you're doing in my library?! You think you can stick your nose in my business without my say-so? ...Oh, don't you dare give me any lip on my turf, little mageling! You think I won't use my fire among my precious books? Things here <i>only </i>burn when I want them to burn, and you're looking awfully flammable to me right now! ...Yeah, I thought you'd reconsider. You want some of my secrets, you gotta pay for it upfront, buddy. I have library cards for that reason.<br /> <br /> Now, where was I?<br /> <br /> Oh, right. On top of managing my library of supernatural secrets and forbidden knowledge, I also have a side gig built up from being active in my local community of monsters. I don't just go places, I can also let people through as well! And beyond that, my blood has got <i>power </i>to it. Those wizards and sorcerers love having me attend their workings, and with a bit of a bloody blessing from me, they've got a lot more dark power to draw upon. Even the werewolves have their own little rituals they observe. Oh, I've gotten some juicy lore from the Shadow in exchange for my help when one of those wolf shamans needed some extra draconic OOMPH to their ritual to kick a spirit's hiney outta here that was more than they could manage on their own.<br /> <br /> So, yes. Considering the evidence of being a <i>fucking</i> dragon, I can only conclude that your argument looks invalid to me. Rawr, baby. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><i>I dreamt I saw a lizard.<br /> <br /> A little lizard.<br /> <br /> It thought its tiny cave was a lair.<br /> <br /> It thought its quiet squeak was a roar.<br /> <br /> It thought its puny spark was fire.<br /> <br /> It thought it was large because all it saw<br /> <br /> were the tinier things around it.</i><br /> <br /> It was wrong.<br /> <br /> Come to me little lizard.<br /> <br /> I was show you a lair and a roar and fire<br /> <br /> I will eat you whole and you will become part of me<br /> <br /> And then you will be large.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T03:42:09-07:00","id":1373876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1373872#post1373872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>I dreamt I saw a lizard.<br /> <br /> A little lizard.<br /> <br /> It thought its tiny cave was a lair.<br /> <br /> It thought its quiet squeak was a roar.<br /> <br /> It thought its puny spark was fire.<br /> <br /> It thought it was large because all it saw<br /> <br /> were the tinier things around it.</i><br /> <br /> It was wrong.<br /> <br /> Come to me little lizard.<br /> <br /> I was show you a lair and a roar and fire<br /> <br /> I will eat you whole and you will become part of me<br /> <br /> And then you will be large.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was pretty happy with my post. With just a few paragraphs I presented an arrogant character making use of their power, having desires and goals, things the character cares about, and how the character pursues their goals in ways that drive a story forward with plenty of opportunities to mix things up with various other characters. It just shows how much Beasts can get around, do some much with many different kinds of people and practically none of it being tied to feeding a Hunger. Or rather, feeding a Hunger is just a side benefit for doing those things....<br /> <br /> And this is what you take from it, I guess.<br /> <br /> I think it would be detrimental to Beast: The Primordial for them to have an external source of antagonistic cosmic dread like you seem to want. And I'll tell you why. The biggest monster a Beast has to fear? Is themselves. Of what they'll become. Beast: The Primordial is strongly hinged on it's inward focus, to the dynamic of struggling with their Satiety, their Hunger, and having to draw lines on what they're willing to do and what they're not willing to do. Having some cosmic external threat detracts from that individual struggle, because the horror of a cosmic threat is that You Are Insignificant and You Don't Matter. But the choices a Beast makes have to matter because that is where the crux of the story lies.<br /> <br /> If you want to know the measure of a person, give them power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T04:25:51-07:00","id":1373884,"title":"","content":"Beast has external fears: both the dominance of mankind and their ongoing arrogance in subjugating the world <i>as</i> avatars of the world, and at the same time being the ones at the front of humanity succumbing to the void and being the front fighters against entropy dressing humanity down. Honestly, Beast suffers <i>too much</i> from it's external horror, and not enough from it's internal horror, because it's internal horror is also really, deeply, it's main draw.<br /> <br /> Beast has <i>the world</i> to pit themselves against, and it clearly needs pitting against with it's state. What's really horrifying about Beast is this notion that if any of them win?<br /> <br /> Some things might change for the better, but not a whole lot is going to change. They possibly empathize <i>too </i>much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T04:43:30-07:00","id":1373887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1373834#post1373834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Damn Arcane, Cinder may be my favourite for essays on Beast, but you're a real close second. Are you making that 1.5 edition for the storyteller vault? I would really like to read it if it involves the Astral (and that would make feel a lot better about building your Legend and how the Horror itself spreads through the collective unconscious of humanity.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't elaborate on background goals at this point, but on any chance this falls, it'll end up playing it's way to the Storyteller Vault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T04:46:32-07:00","id":1373888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1373887#post1373887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I won't elaborate on background goals at this point, but on any chance this falls, it'll end up playing it's way to the Storyteller Vault.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. I'll be looking forward to it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T06:39:04-07:00","id":1373907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1373884#post1373884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, Beast suffers <i>too much</i> from it's external horror, and not enough from it's internal horror, because it's internal horror is also really, deeply, it's main draw.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to pretend like I've thought about this even half as much as everyone else posting in this thread, but this point really resonated with me. When I think about the kind of game I naively wanted from Beast, when it was first announced, my conception was something like you've been marked by a Beast of legend (a Dragon, an Eldritch Horror, etc), and your transformation has begun. I envisioned a game where you can either participate willingly like a cultist, you can struggle against it like a hero, you can try to ignore it like you're in denial, or you can try to claim it like your birthright. The more you feed your beast's hunger, the more you become like it. You don't commit atrocities because you have to in order to survive, but because you're persistently nudged to crave power, and doing so gives you that power, and you *like* power. Instead of the mood being &quot;you're already a monster and you have to hurt people to survive while building up your personal urban myth,&quot; I would have preferred &quot;you're going through monstrous self-discovery and you need to decide what that means.&quot;<br /> <br /> And the frustrating part, like everyone is saying here, is that 95% of that is already there in Beast. It's just... poorly stitched together, and really misses the mark. Some stuff is absolutely grand (combined resource/morality is fun, the various atavisms and nightmares are great, crossover potential is huge), but some decisions just leave me baffled. In particular, I think it's odd that feeding your Hunger abates the Horror. It makes it feel like &quot;oh, I have to satisfy my Hunger in order to put my Horror at ease,&quot; when satisfying your Hunger should be the thing that *drives* your Horror. Even mechanically, the way the game works now, satisfying your Hunger weakens your Atavisms and makes you *less* like the Horror you're feeding. That just feels so antithematic and anticlimactic.<br /> <br /> I didn't want a game world where I could just be a monster. I wanted a game world that would show me why being a monster is appealing. I think that's at the core of what makes Vampire, Werewolf, and even Mage so fun. And it's just kind of missing from the game about actual monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 03-10-2020, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T12:04:30-07:00","id":1373955,"title":"","content":"Ok, I've thought about this even more and I guess I could crystallize my complaints above into three points:<br /> <br /> 1. Giving into your Horror should strengthen it, not abate it<br /> 2. The combined resource/Integrity stat does not have a strong connection to your monstrous activity, and so it feels just like a resource management minigame without the character having any Integrity stat at all<br /> 3. Your character rarely has to confront her actions in any mechanically meaningful way<br /> <br /> I'm not a good enough player/ST to figure out what the answers to those problems are. My naive attempt at a bad possible solution follows: You could design a system that has actual Breaking Points, and you derive power from them somehow. Breaking Points give you Resource, whether or not you lose Integrity. Lower Integrity gives you more power for your Atavisms, but obviously the lower your Integrity, the fewer opportunities for Breaking Points you're going to have. Maybe Resources go into your dice pool for Nightmares, or you can spend them other ways. This system (1) makes you more monstrous when you act more monstrous, (2) incentivizes you to make interesting choices about how far into your monstrosity you dive, and (3) ties your character's personal horror (at the things she does) to her actual Horror.<br /> <br /> I don't think that's a great idea, but it's just one idea that tries to minimally rework things to fix my chief complaints.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T12:30:48-07:00","id":1373971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1373955#post1373955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I've thought about this even more and I guess I could crystallize my complaints above into three points:<br /> <br /> 1. Giving into your Horror should strengthen it, not abate it<br /> 2. The combined resource/Integrity stat does not have a strong connection to your monstrous activity, and so it feels just like a resource management minigame without the character having any Integrity stat at all<br /> 3. Your character rarely has to confront her actions in any mechanically meaningful way<br /> <br /> I'm not a good enough player/ST to figure out what the answers to those problems are. My naive attempt at a bad possible solution follows: You could design a system that has actual Breaking Points, and you derive power from them somehow. Breaking Points give you Resource, whether or not you lose Integrity. Lower Integrity gives you more power for your Atavisms, but obviously the lower your Integrity, the fewer opportunities for Breaking Points you're going to have. Maybe Resources go into your dice pool for Nightmares, or you can spend them other ways. This system (1) makes you more monstrous when you act more monstrous, (2) incentivizes you to make interesting choices about how far into your monstrosity you dive, and (3) ties your character's personal horror (at the things she does) to her actual Horror.<br /> <br /> I don't think that's a great idea, but it's just one idea that tries to minimally rework things to fix my chief complaints.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're missing out on the Satiety Conditions. The Satiety structure is intrinsically tied to the Satiety Conditions and a Beast is <i>always </i>under the effect of one Satiety Condition or another. This is important, because it ties specifically into each of your points. Satiety itself is a resource that strengthens the Beast, enabling the Beast to wield more power. On top of that, whether being Starving or Gorged affects a Beast's power, allowing easier use of Atavisms or Nightmares, accordingly.<br /> <br /> For 2 and 3, Satiety Conditions specifically encourage monstrous behavior that is problematic for the Beast. Gorged makes you more easier to be influenced, while also making the digesting Beast more slothful and prone to failing actions where the Beast should instead be proactive and engaged. Meanwhile, Starving makes the Beast act more irrationally, taking riskier behaviors and engaging in more dangerous activities when pursuing Satiety.<br /> <br /> Satiety isn't a resource management game, it is a mechanic that directly influences the character's behavior with every Condition.<br /> <br /> I think getting away from dealing with Breaking Points was rather helpful to Beast... Not everything needs to mechanically represented, a Beast can still feel horrible about the things they've done, or have a strong code of ethics they believe in and strive to follow. Rather, the lack of Breaking Points for Beasts makes a very interesting statement about Beasts in of themselves. To me, it makes me think of Beasts being able to witness some really frightening or terrible things... But their mind isn't going to break from that alone. They could treat with some mind-shredding extra-dimensional terror, and stand on somewhat firm ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T12:39:05-07:00","id":1373973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1373955#post1373955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I've thought about this even more and I guess I could crystallize my complaints above into three points:<br /> <br /> 1. Giving into your Horror should strengthen it, not abate it</div> </div> </div> </div>It honestly depends on how you're defining the idea of strengthening your Horror. Like your atavisms are strong at low satiety, but that isn't because the Horror is stronger its because its pressing closer to the surface for any food stuff it can get. At the same it doesn't care what it gets, so long as there is food and to that end it is easier to manage your Horror at low Satiety than it is at high Satiety. At higher Satiety the Horror is capable of being picky about what it will eat, so feeding the Horror at higher satiety requires more extreme actions in line with its own wants. You can go much longer without feeding it and not hitting Ravenous, but its capable of inflicting Nightmares more effectively and has Satiety that it can burn for the biggest effects.<br /> <br /> So it is debatable on which would be a stronger. Your Nightmare powers suffer when you haven't been feeding (low satiety) however you gain access to a number of other effects from your atavisms and can only use your satiety effects in dire straits as you don't have much to work with, but the Horror being easier to feed. High satiety your nightmares are powered up, and you don't have some of the stronger powers from your atavisms, with your Horror being pickier about how it eats; but you can go way longer without feeding before you get run the risk of 0 satiety and you have resources to burn to get your best effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T12:48:12-07:00","id":1373975,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Satiety conditions address my point. In fact they're sort of a great example of the symptoms of the problem. You commit great horrors, let's say you even kill your victim, like a real big bad monster. You're literally being the most monstrous you could possibly be! And as a result, you fill your Satiety up to 10 and get the Slumbering condition. Your Horror curls up and goes to sleep (that's literally the description-- curls up and goes to sleep, like a kitten). Like, in the face of the most horrific acts you can commit, your Horror completely abates, and you become practically human. It's weird that you become the most human by acting the most inhumanely.<br /> <br /> I was the first to admit the system I concocted in that post is probably bad, I just wanted to give an example of a kind of system that reinforces the thematic behavior instead of subverting it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T13:39:17-07:00","id":1373982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1373975#post1373975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the Satiety conditions address my point. In fact they're sort of a great example of the symptoms of the problem. You commit great horrors, let's say you even kill your victim, like a real big bad monster. You're literally being the most monstrous you could possibly be! And as a result, you fill your Satiety up to 10 and get the Slumbering condition. Your Horror curls up and goes to sleep (that's literally the description-- curls up and goes to sleep, like a kitten). Like, in the face of the most horrific acts you can commit, your Horror completely abates, and you become practically human. It's weird that you become the most human by acting the most inhumanely.<br /> <br /> I was the first to admit the system I concocted in that post is probably bad, I just wanted to give an example of a kind of system that reinforces the thematic behavior instead of subverting it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're minimizing what the Slumbering Condition does to a Beast. It strips a Beast of all their power that they can use to protect themselves. It strips them of any Atavisms that help keep them informed and knowledgeable. Having the Slumbering Condition is explicitly noted as causing a Beast to feel uncomfortable and suffer from depression.<br /> <br /> Your experience at being &quot;mostly human&quot; is living with yourself feeling diminished, vulnerable, feeling terrible about yourself, having issues with motivation, etc.<br /> <br /> This should not be viewed as a pleasant experience or as if the Beast is being rewarded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T13:52:55-07:00","id":1373989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1373975#post1373975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the Satiety conditions address my point. In fact they're sort of a great example of the symptoms of the problem. You commit great horrors, let's say you even kill your victim, like a real big bad monster. You're literally being the most monstrous you could possibly be! And as a result, you fill your Satiety up to 10 and get the Slumbering condition. Your Horror curls up and goes to sleep (that's literally the description-- curls up and goes to sleep, like a kitten). Like, in the face of the most horrific acts you can commit, your Horror completely abates, and you become practically human. It's weird that you become the most human by acting the most inhumanely.<br /> <br /> I was the first to admit the system I concocted in that post is probably bad, I just wanted to give an example of a kind of system that reinforces the thematic behavior instead of subverting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like you want an Insatiable more than anything. Beasts are monsters, sure, but you know how in the stories, the monster isnt just rampantly causing destruction? The dragon in Beowulf had its stuff stolen and was sleeping, the mermaids (or are they also called harpies in these myths?) take one sailor down to the depths with them to be devoured, but only ever need just one, and even more recent stories like Slenderman arent mindlessly killing in mass but picking carefully?<br /> <br /> If beasts just kill and have no cap, they are just insatiable, no longer can there be reason to their legend, no longer can a lesson truly be attached. It's like charybdis, the greek monster who was more whirlpool than monster. You could learn, at most, &quot;dont go near there&quot;, because that was all the monster did, mindlessly consume, never sated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T16:14:50-07:00","id":1374005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1373876#post1373876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was pretty happy with my post. With just a few paragraphs I presented an arrogant character making use of their power, having desires and goals, things the character cares about, and how the character pursues their goals in ways that drive a story forward with plenty of opportunities to mix things up with various other characters. It just shows how much Beasts can get around, do some much with many different kinds of people and practically none of it being tied to feeding a Hunger. Or rather, feeding a Hunger is just a side benefit for doing those things....<br /> <br /> And this is what you take from it, I guess.<br /> <br /> I think it would be detrimental to Beast: The Primordial for them to have an external source of antagonistic cosmic dread like you seem to want. And I'll tell you why. The biggest monster a Beast has to fear? Is themselves. Of what they'll become. Beast: The Primordial is strongly hinged on it's inward focus, to the dynamic of struggling with their Satiety, their Hunger, and having to draw lines on what they're willing to do and what they're not willing to do. Having some cosmic external threat detracts from that individual struggle, because the horror of a cosmic threat is that You Are Insignificant and You Don't Matter. But the choices a Beast makes have to matter because that is where the crux of the story lies.<br /> <br /> If you want to know the measure of a person, give them power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked your Dragon story. The reaction I posted would what Typhon might relate. A few people have called Beast, Dark Scion. That's part of my take as well. One thing to remember about Scion is that it takes place amid a backdrop of conflict with the Titans. Your Dragon story gave an excellent view of Beast who wants to build his Legend. It's understandable why some Beasts would want to build their Legend.<br /> <br /> Typhon is the answer to &quot;Why do a Beasts <i>need</i> to build their Legends?&quot; While it might start as Cosmic Horror, the Typhon concept is when cosmic horror tells Beasts &quot;You Are Insignificant&quot; and &quot;You Don't Matter&quot; the Beasts retort &quot;We are Significant. We do matter. I am the Dragon Under than Mountain, the Fire in the Sky at Night. The Forsaken wolves cry out my name. The will-workers bring me into their working to empower them and the mortals below look to the sky and shudder. You, thing in the Abyss are just a dream that deludes itself into believing it's still relevant.&quot;<br /> <br /> In the normal way of things, Typhon and his creations feed on the quiet dreads of the sentient. The nameless, unspoken fears. Beasts make those fears manifest, embody them and draw that power to themselves and away from Typhon. As a Beast you build your Legend and push your power not simply for yourself, but to take it away from Typhon. To reduce him. To finally make him feel the Cosmic Horror that he is insignificant and he does not matter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T16:21:27-07:00","id":1374007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1374005#post1374005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I liked your Dragon story. The reaction I posted would what Typhon might relate. A few people have called Beast, Dark Scion. That's part of my take as well. One thing to remember about Scion is that it takes place amid a backdrop of conflict with the Titans. Your Dragon story gave an excellent view of Beast who wants to build his Legend. It's understandable why some Beasts would want to build their Legend.<br /> <br /> Typhon is the answer to &quot;Why do a Beasts <i>need</i> to build their Legends?&quot; While it might start as Cosmic Horror, the Typhon concept is when cosmic horror tells Beasts &quot;You Are Insignificant&quot; and &quot;You Don't Matter&quot; the Beasts retort &quot;We are Significant. We do matter. I am the Dragon Under than Mountain, the Fire in the Sky at Night. The Forsaken wolves cry out my name. The will-workers bring me into their working to empower them and the mortals below look to the sky and shudder. You, thing in the Abyss are just a dream that deludes itself into believing it's still relevant.&quot;<br /> <br /> In the normal way of things, Typhon and his creations feed on the quiet dreads of the sentient. The nameless, unspoken fears. Beasts make those fears manifest, embody them and draw that power to themselves and away from Typhon. As a Beast you build your Legend and push your power not simply for yourself, but to take it away from Typhon. To reduce him. To finally make him feel the Cosmic Horror that he is insignificant and he does not matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...That's actually a really good response. Thank you for taking the time to make it. That's something for me to think about.<br /> <br /> Edit: I guess a concern I have for having some external threat being &quot;why&quot; Beasts need to build their Legends is... It provides an external justification for what they do and.... I feel that's kind of dangerous. Beasts feeding their Hungers should never have an objective justification proving them in the right for the awful things they do to feed those Hungers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 03-10-2020, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T17:47:41-07:00","id":1374025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1374005#post1374005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I liked your Dragon story. The reaction I posted would what Typhon might relate. A few people have called Beast, Dark Scion. That's part of my take as well. One thing to remember about Scion is that it takes place amid a backdrop of conflict with the Titans. Your Dragon story gave an excellent view of Beast who wants to build his Legend. It's understandable why some Beasts would want to build their Legend.<br /> <br /> Typhon is the answer to &amp;quot;Why do a Beasts <i>need</i> to build their Legends?&amp;quot; While it might start as Cosmic Horror, the Typhon concept is when cosmic horror tells Beasts &amp;quot;You Are Insignificant&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;You Don't Matter&amp;quot; the Beasts retort &amp;quot;We are Significant. We do matter. I am the Dragon Under than Mountain, the Fire in the Sky at Night. The Forsaken wolves cry out my name. The will-workers bring me into their working to empower them and the mortals below look to the sky and shudder. You, thing in the Abyss are just a dream that deludes itself into believing it's still relevant.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> In the normal way of things, Typhon and his creations feed on the quiet dreads of the sentient. The nameless, unspoken fears. Beasts make those fears manifest, embody them and draw that power to themselves and away from Typhon. As a Beast you build your Legend and push your power not simply for yourself, but to take it away from Typhon. To reduce him. To finally make him feel the Cosmic Horror that he is insignificant and he does not matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>3 problems with this<br /> <br /> 1. If Typhon is a &quot;Cosmic Horror&quot;, and father (or however he relates to the begotten) to Beasts, what is beasts' connection to humanity? The dark mother and beasts are probably the least human, at the same level as demon, even. But, they are, paradoxically, the supernatural template most tied into humanity for they represent human fears (wish I knew how to italicize for emphasis). To have them tied to a cosmic horror figure takes away that connection. Representing quiet dread, which typhon seems to make from himself, rather than fears humanity had that were then personified, makes the begotten much different from what they are now.<br /> <br /> 2. Typhon is nothing new to the chronicles of darkness. He seems to be a more personable God machine, telling beast they arent anything in the grand scheme of things, much like demons feel when they arent Angels anymore. Much like what paradim pointed out, we are giving what was once an internal struggle a source to push the blame on <br /> <br /> 3. This goes along with he first part of issue 2. The Dark Mother is unique in the chronicles of darkness. We have our amoral, 4D chess playing god (god machine), tyrannical god kings bent on enslavement of humanity (Exarchs), a distant, unknowable entity enacting great change upon the world (The Principle), insane deities using people as playthings, and a dead god that has forever left its mark upon the world (Father Wolf, his mark being the Uratha). What we are missing, is a deity closely tied with its offspring, one that is never seen but felt throughout the game. A figure that serves as an anchor and emotional crutch, rather than an antagonist or manipulator. The Dark Mother IS that. That's what makes her unique from the others<br /> <br /> Ok, I di have one more. That feeling you want, you can already have that. The guardian beasts think of the dark mother as an abusive parent. They even believe Incarnation is the beast asserting themselves independently from the dark mother, weakening her","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T18:14:13-07:00","id":1374028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1374007#post1374007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...That's actually a really good response. Thank you for taking the time to make it. That's something for me to think about.<br /> <br /> Edit: I guess a concern I have for having some external threat being &quot;why&quot; Beasts need to build their Legends is... It provides an external justification for what they do and.... I feel that's kind of dangerous. Beasts feeding their Hungers should never have an objective justification proving them in the right for the awful things they do to feed those Hungers.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not exactly about justification so much as necessity.<br /> <br /> Here's Bob. Bob is Beast with a Hunger for Power. Bob is a Manager at a local grocery. He Feeds by bullying and lording it over employees (making them work through lunch, take unpaid overtime, bring the shopping carts in during a pouring rain despite the lack of rain gear). Bob is an asshole and by being an asshole he's pretty much able to remain at Sated or Gorged most of the time. He's got a small Lair (maybe three areas) and doesn't do anything really big enough to attract Heroes' attention. He's your basic asshole boss and as such doesn't really attract a bunch of attention because asshole bosses are more common than dirt in the NWoD. And he's actually a slight improvement over the previous human manager who tried to push the teenage girls into sex acts.<br /> <br /> So, game stuff aside, Bob is sitting pretty and there's really not much reason for him to push his Legend, grow his Lair or otherwise rock his particular Beastly boat in a normal Beast set-up.<br /> <br /> With Typhon, there is. Lilith Begot her Beastly children with the intent that they would drain Typhon's power and pull him off his throne as Kind-of-the-Mountain/Lord-of-the-Abyss. He knows that. Insatiable are His creations, sent forth to stoke fears and also go after Beasts. Heroes are Oracles that Typhon has twisted through the Primordial Dream. They actively hunt for Beasts using the Dark Gifts of Typhon (though they are unwitting pawns of his). <br /> <br /> Instead of being random, almost incidental dangers to Beasts, Heroes and the Insatiable are (again, mostly unwitting) agents of their ultimate enemy.<br /> <br /> So instead of enjoying his relatively safe niche as well-fed Horror/Asshole Boss, Bob needs to start building his Lair and Legend because he's being hunted. And if he's not ready, those hunters will sniff him out and snuff him out.<br /> <br /> Of course, even as a monster, you can still decide what kind of monster you'll be. Godzilla and Mothra are monsters, but the Japanese were super-glad they were around when King Ghidorah showed up and started breaking the furniture around Tokyo.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'd kind of like Beasts to have a version of the Integrity trait to reflect that Beasts are human and Horror and that a balance should be maintained between them. Call it Bonding unless that's used elsewhere. The higher Bonding is the better control the Beast has over his Hunger and Atavisms. A Low Bonding leaves the Beast - especially his Horror, open to the blandishments of Typhon. Quite a few of the Insatiable used to <i>be</i> Beasts before they fell to Typhon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T18:28:09-07:00","id":1374030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1374028#post1374028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not exactly about justification so much as necessity.<br /> <br /> Here's Bob. Bob is Beast with a Hunger for Power. Bob is a Manager at a local grocery. He Feeds by bullying and lording it over employees (making them work through lunch, take unpaid overtime, bring the shopping carts in during a pouring rain despite the lack of rain gear). Bob is an asshole and by being an asshole he's pretty much able to remain at Sated or Gorged most of the time. He's got a small Lair (maybe three areas) and doesn't do anything really big enough to attract Heroes' attention. He's your basic asshole boss and as such doesn't really attract a bunch of attention because asshole bosses are more common than dirt in the NWoD. And he's actually a slight improvement over the previous human manager who tried to push the teenage girls into sex acts.<br /> <br /> So, game stuff aside, Bob is sitting pretty and there's really not much reason for him to push his Legend, grow his Lair or otherwise rock his particular Beastly boat in a normal Beast set-up.<br /> <br /> With Typhon, there is. Lilith Begot her Beastly children with the intent that they would drain Typhon's power and pull him off his throne as Kind-of-the-Mountain/Lord-of-the-Abyss. He knows that. Insatiable are His creations, sent forth to stoke fears and also go after Beasts. Heroes are Oracles that Typhon has twisted through the Primordial Dream. They actively hunt for Beasts using the Dark Gifts of Typhon (though they are unwitting pawns of his). <br /> <br /> Instead of being random, almost incidental dangers to Beasts, Heroes and the Insatiable are (again, mostly unwitting) agents of their ultimate enemy.<br /> <br /> So instead of enjoying his relatively safe niche as well-fed Horror/Asshole Boss, Bob needs to start building his Lair and Legend because he's being hunted. And if he's not ready, those hunters will sniff him out and snuff him out.<br /> <br /> Of course, even as a monster, you can still decide what kind of monster you'll be. Godzilla and Mothra are monsters, but the Japanese were super-glad they were around when King Ghidorah showed up and started breaking the furniture around Tokyo.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'd kind of like Beasts to have a version of the Integrity trait to reflect that Beasts are human and Horror and that a balance should be maintained between them. Call it Bonding unless that's used elsewhere. The higher Bonding is the better control the Beast has over his Hunger and Atavisms. A Low Bonding leaves the Beast - especially his Horror, open to the blandishments of Typhon. Quite a few of the Insatiable used to <i>be</i> Beasts before they fell to Typhon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Realistically, Bob's business would go down, everyone would just quit. Now Bob has a problem, a problem caused by his own innate nature and lacking foresight into the consequences.<br /> <br /> You cant just disregard that the actions of a beast have consequences. And what Bob is doing will forever keep him on low satiety, which will make him erratic, and at best sated. And with his life, he is fucked if a Hero notices him. <br /> <br /> Again, Heroes are now losing their intrinsic link with Beasts. No longer are they tied to beasts and serve as a walking crisis of identity with their own issues. Now they are just pawns. That's a loss of depth.<br /> <br /> I simply dont see why this external threat need to be here. It actually changes a LOT more about beasts when looked into. As for integrity, beasts are monsters that represent fears. A big part of beast is that morality is a detached idea. Hell, the Horror does not give a shit about morality l, it IS a selfish monster that only cares to feed. Morality is for the beast to decide, and that influences their legend. Hiw they come with that, how humanity perceives their actions...they can only hope for the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T18:38:49-07:00","id":1374032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1374028#post1374028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not exactly about justification so much as necessity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The most terrible kinds of things have been done, justified as being &quot;necessity&quot;.<br /> <br /> The worst thing that could happen to Beast: The Primordial is to present their Hungers as objectively justified. That's... I can't go along with that, or anything that even hints at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T19:56:04-07:00","id":1374047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1374005#post1374005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Typhon is the answer to &quot;Why do a Beasts <i>need</i> to build their Legends?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>1) You don't need Typhon when you have Insatiables though, but more importantly<br /> <br /> 2) The answer to &quot;Why do Beasts need to build their Lair/Legend?&quot; is once again already answered, all that needs to happen is properly contextualize that answer-The Devouring.<br /> <br /> The Devouring is not a small event in anyone's personal life, it is a signficant actualization of persona and shadow by combining the person's Soul and the primordial Horror, coming home to their self. While,yes kids, actualization is not a singular matter, the important thing about this fulfillment is that it's significant enough that Beasts now have the final part of Maslow's Hierarchy of Needs open to them as a thing to chase, and that's self-transcendence, taking this completed aspect of self and manifesting it in the world, making it a <i>part</i> of the world. The nature of Hunger and feelings of Kinship and the way those directly contribute to the Lair take that feeling that transcendence is the next step and manifests the reality of it as action.<br /> <br /> Beasts build Lair/Legend because that is how they are driven, because it's the next logical step for their journey, in becoming who they are.<br /> <br /> And keeping that in places helps to preserve and emphasize the internal horror of the characters and the moral stance of the game-Beasts <i>are</i> villain protagonists, Primordial is a morally dark grey game with murky ethics no easy answer for it's central conflict, and the characters always have some kind of shade of &quot;terrible person&quot; to them that also helps to make player decision towards aspirationally good and event contributive action and being that much more meaningful. It lets Beasts own themselves <i>as monsters</i> in a way that isn't done in a lot of other games and is one of the big aspects of why people like this game-their accountability as Beasts both damns and frees them, and the question of how to take self and contribute to community, or the question contributing to community is even desirable, is very compelling for the fanbase.<br /> <br /> You don't need an outside reason for Beasts to be Beasts. You just have make the transgression, the camaraderie, and the mythic approach of the game clearly understandable in a way that is also fun, and ideally also clear as a mean for reflection, contemplation, and discussion.<br /> <br /> So, no, I still see no need for Typhon. Besides, we already have a Typhon as an Aeon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T20:28:59-07:00","id":1374052,"title":"","content":"Also, not to put too fine a point on it, Incarnate Beasts are already easily capable of equaling or surpassing top tier threats for some splats, and most things beyond that are more in the realm of abstract concepts rather than embodied entities that one can meaningfully interact with directly.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, you already have a world full of existential antagonists to choose from and it's far more interesting to look at the whole wide world of monsters and decide for yourself, yes, these ones I will help and these ones I will fight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T23:02:37-07:00","id":1374073,"title":"","content":"The Bob example also isn't really a Beast specific problem.<br /> <br /> All the gamelines have the potential to design a character that effectively sits around having a quiet life, maintaining their needs and keeping under the radar.<br /> <br /> Those aren't PCs though, because we play the games to have drama and conflict. We understand that our characters might want to be Bob, we as players and the ST know that our characters aren't going to be allowed to have that life because that doesn't make for a fun game.<br /> <br /> Vampire focuses on cities because playing the lone vampire that controls a small town of ~10K people, doesn't have competition from other vampires, isn't overlapping territory with other supernaturals, and isn't causing enough of a fuss for hunters or Strix to even care that they exist, isn't terribly interesting. That doesn't mean Vampire Bob here can't exist, and thus poses a problem for Vampire. It just means it's not the default mode of play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T10:01:04-07:00","id":1374159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1374047#post1374047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) You don't need Typhon when you have Insatiables though, but more importantly...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really about need, though. How many antagonists are really needed by other games. In Werewolf, you could reasonably dump the Pure/Idigam/Bale Hounds and run it as a furrier &quot;Game of Thrones&quot; with the inheritors of Father Wolf struggling over his legacy and squabbling for territory. But those beings deepen the world, up the stakes and provide common enemies to help unite the various tribes and packs.<br /> <br /> Beasts are the Begotten. Not the Embraces, Created, Awakened, etc. On a metaphorical/Dream level, Lilith fucked someone and Beasts were the ultimate result.<br /> <br /> One of the themes in Beast is that of family. Beasts are &quot;siblings&quot; of a sort. Other supernaturals are &quot;cousins&quot; for the most part (Demons being the exception).<br /> <br /> Lilith is the Mother. You are the Monster that she, as a Mother, can love.<br /> <br /> Typhon is the Father and you, as a Beast, are his child as well. You are of him. Your Horror is shpaed by him. And if you want to progess, protect yourself, make a difference, you have to Feed the Hunger that are of him.<br /> <br /> While it seems like Cosmic Horror, Typhon has a personal effect on Beasts. Typhon is every abusive, cruel, asshole parent that every child who was victimized by swears they will never, ever be like. And yet many end up being very much like. Satiety 10 is awful because getting to it requires indulging that dark, vicious part of yourself, and when the Horror takes a nap the Human that's left confronts himself with that knowledge, much like what happens when the child of an alcoholic wakes up after bender, realizing she fucked up just like dear 'ol Dad used to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1374047#post1374047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, no, I still see no need for Typhon. Besides, we already have a Typhon as an Aeon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what an Aeon is in this context.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T10:29:46-07:00","id":1374164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1374159#post1374159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know what an Aeon is in this context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Extremely powerful beings from the Anima Mundi, possibly the roots of various Families.<br /> <br /> Typhon in particular is the Aeon of Death, and he's been having his children work to destroy the traditional route into the Dreamtime from the Temenos for some time now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T10:59:22-07:00","id":1374171,"title":"","content":"There comes a point in the talking it becomes clear a person doesn't know what they talking about, and I am probably far later in approaching that boundary than I should be.<br /> <br /> In the meantime.<br /> <br /> 1) The Dark Mother fucked a lot more than one entity to start the Families. The BPG pluralizes Progenitor-Beasts for a reason, and there is a dynamic reason both Doylistically and Watsonianly for this multiple spouse thing.<br /> <br /> 2) Your Typhon continues to serve purposes that are better served externally by The Insatiable the Deities of the Mother's Land and internally by the consequences of the Devouring and the natural result Astral metaphysics.<br /> <br /> Again, Beast has everything it needs to be a great game. All it needs is correct contextualization and presentation.<br /> <br /> Typhon doesn't contribute anything Beast doesn't already do better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T11:45:32-07:00","id":1374178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1374171#post1374171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There comes a point in the talking it becomes clear a person doesn't know what they talking about, and I am probably far later in approaching that boundary than I should be.<br /> <br /> In the meantime.<br /> <br /> 1) The Dark Mother fucked a lot more than one entity to start the Families. The BPG pluralizes Progenitor-Beasts for a reason, and there is a dynamic reason both Doylistically and Watsonianly for this multiple spouse thing.<br /> <br /> 2) Your Typhon continues to serve purposes that are better served externally by The Insatiable the Deities of the Mother's Land and internally by the consequences of the Devouring and the natural result Astral metaphysics.<br /> <br /> Again, Beast has everything it needs to be a great game. All it needs is correct contextualization and presentation.<br /> <br /> Typhon doesn't contribute anything Beast doesn't already do better.</div> </div> </div> </div>And to add, The beast relationship to Typhon sounds like the Pure to Luna, but with extra steps","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T11:50:10-07:00","id":1374181,"title":"","content":"Look if you want a big storyline for Beasts, no god monsters or the like beyond what's already there. The angle is simple. <b> The world has moved on. </b> Beasts had a role they used to fulfill, ages back there was a balance, the Beghotten were the fears and the monsters that humanity needed to understand the less friendly lessons there were. It doesn't matter how strong or fast you are the avalanche will crush you when you get caught in it, for example. And there was a balance, the Heroes, those who's job it was to go in and educate the common folk on how to avoid being caught in the avalanche and to deal with those Beasts that cross the line into just being dangers to humanity. Still the world has gone on, things have changed. A Beast's counterpoint now seems only to exist to slaughter them when the Beasts are found. The monster inside doesn't even consider the idea of a line and just wants to rampage regardless of whether it would teach anyone anything.<br /> <br /> So, what do you do? Are the lessons your kind used to teach still needed? Do you just need a new method of teaching? Should you throw in with the other parts of the family and bring your talents to their enterprises? You exist, you have desires, and needs just like everyone else. (Even if those needs and desires involve making a bed in the collective unconscious out of a pile of wealth taken from those who crossed you.) So why do you exist, why do more of your kind keep getting made, and where do you fit into the world now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T13:11:04-07:00","id":1374206,"title":"","content":"I know that I would dearly love new material on what the Astral Realms are like for Beasts and more exploration on them. The stuff in the Player's Guide really feels like the tip of the iceberg and I'd really love more material on inhabitants and what can happen there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T19:48:01-07:00","id":1374279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1374206#post1374206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that I would dearly love new material on what the Astral Realms are like for Beasts and more exploration on them. The stuff in the Player's Guide really feels like the tip of the iceberg and I'd really love more material on inhabitants and what can happen there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I mean, I REALLY love the players guide. It gives an incredibly clear idea on the Begotten culture and what it's like to be one. But being the astral residents who can make modern legends in dreams of humanity, Beast: the primordial is the only game besides werewolf where I'm just as interested in the alternate world as I am with the monsters themselves (and by alternate world, I mean the Shadow and Astral/primordial dream)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T19:51:44-07:00","id":1374282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1374279#post1374279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. I mean, I REALLY love the players guide. It gives an incredibly clear idea on the Begotten culture and what it's like to be one. But being the astral residents who can make modern legends in dreams of humanity, Beast: the primordial is the only game besides werewolf where I'm just as interested in the alternate world as I am with the monsters themselves (and by alternate world, I mean the Shadow and Astral/primordial dream)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Something I would kind of like is if there were some threats in the Astral Realms that could threaten a Beast's Lair or be other kinds of threats that Beasts have to deal with. I'd be concerned with making something too similar to the Spirits and Werewolves' Territory sort of dynamic but.... There's a lot of room that could be used here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T05:08:35-07:00","id":1374326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1374181#post1374181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look if you want a big storyline for Beasts, no god monsters or the like beyond what's already there. The angle is simple. <b> The world has moved on. </b> Beasts had a role they used to fulfill, ages back there was a balance, the Beghotten were the fears and the monsters that humanity needed to understand the less friendly lessons there were. It doesn't matter how strong or fast you are the avalanche will crush you when you get caught in it, for example. And there was a balance, the Heroes, those who's job it was to go in and educate the common folk on how to avoid being caught in the avalanche and to deal with those Beasts that cross the line into just being dangers to humanity. Still the world has gone on, things have changed. A Beast's counterpoint now seems only to exist to slaughter them when the Beasts are found. The monster inside doesn't even consider the idea of a line and just wants to rampage regardless of whether it would teach anyone anything.<br /> <br /> So, what do you do? Are the lessons your kind used to teach still needed? Do you just need a new method of teaching? Should you throw in with the other parts of the family and bring your talents to their enterprises? You exist, you have desires, and needs just like everyone else. (Even if those needs and desires involve making a bed in the collective unconscious out of a pile of wealth taken from those who crossed you.) So why do you exist, why do more of your kind keep getting made, and where do you fit into the world now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I would lean away from describing Beasts and Heroes as being relics of an older age that don't neccesarily belong in the modern world. The world is still a relevant force in our lives-we are very subject to nature-and everyone has their own ruling mythologies that grow and evolve and impart values and taboos to themselves and others. The forces that make up the Primordial are omnipresent, just with new forms draped over the old archetypes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364485-fan-re-write-of-beast?p=1374206#post1374206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that I would dearly love new material on what the Astral Realms are like for Beasts and more exploration on them. The stuff in the Player's Guide really feels like the tip of the iceberg and I'd really love more material on inhabitants and what can happen there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah. More space on the Astral ecosystem is highly needed. The big question is if the big exploration should in the BSG or in a Mysterious/Weird Places style book. But you could almost (and probably should) have another Night Horrors book with a significant focus on the the Dreamborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}